    {
      "id": "claim_9431914a87474b17b52929b9cdfb9d64",
      "statement": "The Dockerfile orders the expensive, rarely-changing steps (python3/pip apt install, pip3 install -r requirements.txt, playwright install --with-deps chromium ffmpeg, fonts apt install) before `COPY apps/ .` and the final chown so BuildKit reuses unchanged layers: a requirements.txt change re-runs pip and all later layers, a code-only apps/ change re-runs only the final COPY + chown, and rebuilding the same tree is all-CACHED; the build deliberately carries no per-commit ARG (a Dockerfile ARG value is part of the BuildKit cache key of every RUN step), and the deployed commit is recorded in the deploy log (deploy_remote.sh prints `git log -1`), not as an image label.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CHANGELOG.md#L14-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6332435e24b36e9f3daf592a2d39babd26909c5eac2978a2bd40fb1fbe2e9127:"
        },
