        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c99deb488ce94efd9d1364af0a09d6c7",
      "statement": "After a successful build, install_docker-image.sh replaces apps/Downloads and apps/db with symlinks to CONSUMER_DIR and DB_DIR — a real, non-empty directory is never replaced (it would destroy local data; symlinks from previous installs and empty directories are) and a refusal aborts with a pointer to SKIP_MOUNT_SETUP=1 — and then chowns CONSUMER_DIR and DB_DIR to ${APP_UID}:${APP_GID} so the container's non-root user can write them; a chown failure aborts the deploy rather than surfacing at the next cron run. SKIP_MOUNT_SETUP=1 skips the symlink + chown step entirely for local image builds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://install_docker-image.sh#L115-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d6cfa0edbc18bea63b72574347eb5de2804f23c365468c0d171260b1f1bf5ff6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d6b67fd353d042e99e14c2f5023fbdcc",
      "statement": "deploy_remote.sh reads a root-level .env (template .env.example) and aborts if it is missing or lacks REMOTE_USER, REMOTE_HOST, REMOTE_PATH, INSTALL_SCRIPT, or GIT_BRANCH; over one SSH session it verifies the target directory and git, performs a tag-aware reset (GIT_BRANCH starting with `v` does `git fetch --tags origin` + `git reset --hard <tag>`, making re-running the script the one-command rollback; any other value does `git fetch origin <branch>` + `git reset --hard origin/<branch>`), prints `git log -1` of the deployed commit into the deploy log, forwards CONSUMER_DIR/DB_DIR as exported variables (empty values fall back to the .env next to the script on the remote), and runs INSTALL_SCRIPT with INSTALL_SCRIPT_ARGS.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.env.example#L1-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:880fb6ea1c22ee50cf9ff8bc02f4d8e2324ffed635ba4ab009c408b5720753f4:"
